1. Primary data series (acquired data):
Time (s), displacement (mm), temperature (°C) values for each sensor (including heating-up and cooling-down phases), and  force (kN, only during test load application).
2. Processed data series:
- Processed data regarding the loading phase (see files "Vh5205_C-*-Loading.LIS") and  the creep deformation (see the corresponding LIS file for each test piece).
- The data series from the heating-up and cooling down phases are not provided. Instead, relevant metadata values (rows 34 and 35 for each test piece in the corresponding worksheet) are provided.
- For both loading and creep data the displacement (extension) values (mm) are converted to percentage extension values (%) using the appropiate reference length (determined at room temperature after applying the extensometer according to pre-force).
2.1 Loading data
- The time series values (s) start from t = 0 for better representation of the data.
- The force data values do not include the preload.
2.2 Creep data
- This is the data after the end of the loading, which corresponds to the creep deformation. 
- The time series values (s) are converted to h. The time t = 0 (point b in Figure NA.1 of DIN EN ISO 204:2019-4) corresponds to the time at which the full force of the initial stress is applied to the test piece (start of creep deformation), as specified in DIN EN ISO 204:2019-4.
- The percentage extension values consider an estimation of the extension caused by the preload.
- The temperature values (°C) correspond to the corrected temperature values, which take into account the deviations determined during calibration.






















